    "avatarUrl": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/ERFLGiok6oasJHEMp3Yp6o2VKqafsUj-FPQeEYQVBikv-WsOwE5pXE1bqNI-Fby_VmCS1XVDvEn5a1eEekUaerVa1EbGz6xCVfRcsQzaWS2tFSFoLV4bcUYetNcVkenLUbjb87nn3XEwl6ctIPIKzEBKwhlZu-B7ll228b_kQ_I?purpose=inline",
    "whoWasThisPerson": "A 31-year-old postgraduate medical trainee in her second year of residency in Chest Medicine at RG Kar Medical College and Hospital, Kolkata. Dedicated to clinical pulmonology, she managed demanding shifts in public respiratory wards while preparing for a lifelong career in medical practice. Her story reminds society that healthcare trainees deserve a safe and dignified environment to pursue their vocation.",
    "contributions": "She served frontline clinical duties caring for patients with acute and chronic respiratory illnesses in public hospital wards. UltimateHealth honours her memory through dedicated respiratory education, clinical guidance, and awareness of workplace safety for all healthcare professionals.",
    "factualContext": "On 9 August 2024, after completing an arduous 36-hour clinical shift at RG Kar Medical College and Hospital, she was attacked and murdered in the hospital seminar room while resting. The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) took over the criminal investigation under court order. The Supreme Court of India initiated suo motu proceedings (SMW (Crl) No. 2/2024) and established a 10-member National Task Force to formulate a national safety protocol for healthcare personnel.",
    "societalImpact": "Her loss galvanized unprecedented nationwide strikes by resident doctors and medical associations across India, demanding institutional workplace protection. The Supreme Court initiated suo motu proceedings and constituted a National Task Force — a landmark step toward mandatory occupational safety standards in public hospitals.",
    "verificationStatus": "Verified",
    "lastVerifiedAt": "2026-11-06",
